    "text": "Right, mine just moved the leak to the bottom. Your three types zero it.\n\nTwo things follow from them. The ±6 foils wobble by 12 cents, not 6, so the outer types are easier than the middle one, and a pooled score mixes two difficulties. And scoring by set type does more than separate them: a listener ranking first steps scores perfectly on whichever type their rank rule matches and nothing on the others, while one actually hearing the even split should do about as well on all three, or better on the outer ones. So the breakdown checks for the leak as well as closing it."
